  "prediction": "**Apple's Decision to Remove Headphone Jack Sparks Outrage**\n\nAt the recent Apple keynote event, the company announced the removal of the standard 3.5mm aux cable input, also known as the headphone jack, from its latest iPhone 7 model. Marketing chief Phil Schiller explained the decision by stating that it was a matter of \"courage\" to move on and do something better for all users. However, this explanation was met with widespread mockery and criticism on social media.\n\nCritics argue that removing the headphone jack is a step backward, as it forces users to rely on proprietary wireless technology or expensive dongles to listen to music. The decision has been compared to San Francisco's gentrification of the middle class, where the city's efforts to modernize have led to the displacement of long-time residents.\n\nSeveral experts have pointed out that there is no technological excuse for removing the headphone jack, as music does not sound better over a Lightning cable or wireless technology. In fact, wired audio is often preferred for its superior sound quality.\n\nThe removal of the headphone jack has also raised concerns about the impact on other devices that rely on the jack, such as Square's credit card dongle, temperature sensors, light meters, thermal imaging cameras, and personal breathalyzers.\n\nApple's decision has been seen as a move to further entrench its walled garden ecosystem, where users are forced to purchase proprietary accessories and services. The company's mantra of \"it just works\" has been officially dead, as users are now required to navigate a complex system of dongles and wireless technology to use their devices.\n\nThe backlash against Apple's decision has been fierce, with many users expressing their outrage and frustration on social media. The company's decision to remove the headphone jack has been seen as a symbol of its increasing arrogance and disregard for user needs.\n\nIn response to the criticism, Apple has touted its AirPods as a convenient and seamless solution for wireless audio. However, many users have expressed concerns about the cost and practicality of the AirPods, which retail for $159.\n\nOverall, Apple's decision to remove the headphone jack has sparked a heated debate about the company's priorities and its impact on users. While some may see it as a bold move towards innovation, others view it as a step backward that prioritizes profit over user needs.",
